-# locals: set_id (String), sentinel (Sentinel|nil), groups (Array<[id, name]>)
-#
-# The Set edit page's Derivative access tab. Authors this Set's per-tier policy
-# and, separately, sweeps it across the Works the Set already holds.
-#
-# Saving and applying are two blocks rather than two buttons in a row, because
-# they are two different things and the difference is the point of the tab: a
-# Collection's policy stamps new deposits and is never retroactive, so nothing
-# else in the app changes a rendition that already exists. Putting Apply in the
-# same button row as Save would read as one action with a stray extra control.
-#
-# The ladder itself is the shared partial the Collection tab uses. What differs
-# is the open option: a Collection is a container whose visibility caps its
-# Works, so there its renditions inherit the collection; a Set is not, so here
-# they inherit each Work.
.py-2.px-1
  = bootstrap_form_tag(url: sentinel_set_path(set_id), method: :patch) do |f|
    .well.p-3.my-3.rounded-3
      %h5.mb-1 Derivative access
      %p.small.text-muted.mb-0
        Restrict which groups may download each rendition of this set's works. A rendition you
        don't restrict inherits the visibility of the work it belongs to. Image visibility must
        narrow as resolution grows, so a rendition can't be more open than a smaller one above it.
        Audio, video, and PDF renditions gate on their own.
    %section.my-3{ data: { controller: "derivative-policy", "derivative-policy-groups-value": derivative_group_registry(groups) } }
      %h6.derivative-group-heading Image renditions
      %ol.derivative-ladder.list-unstyled.mb-4
        - Sentinel::IMAGE_LADDER.each do |tier|
          = render "shared/derivative_tier", tier: tier, sentinel: sentinel, groups: groups, open_label: "Inherit from the work"
      %h6.derivative-group-heading Other renditions
      %ul.derivative-independent.list-unstyled.mb-0
        - Sentinel::INDEPENDENT.each do |tier|
          = render "shared/derivative_tier", tier: tier, sentinel: sentinel, groups: groups, open_label: "Inherit from the work"
    .well.p-3.my-3.rounded-3
      = f.button "Save policy", type: :submit, class: "btn btn-success"
      = link_to "Cancel", set_path(set_id), class: "btn btn-warning"

  .well.p-3.my-3.rounded-3
    %h5.mb-1 Apply it to this set's works
    %p.small.text-muted.mb-3
      Saving the policy above does not change anything already in this set. Apply it to write the
      policy onto every work the set holds now. Each rendition is narrowed to what its own work
      allows, so a private work's renditions are withheld rather than refused. You'll get a message
      when it finishes.
    - if sentinel.nil?
      %p.small.text-muted.mb-0
        %i.fa-solid.fa-circle-info.me-1{ 'aria-hidden' => 'true' }
        Save a policy first.
    - else
      = button_to "Apply to this set's works", apply_sentinel_set_path(set_id),
                  class: "btn btn-primary", form: { class: "d-inline" },
                  data: { turbo_confirm: "Apply this policy to every work in this set? Renditions that are currently downloadable may stop being downloadable. You can change the policy and apply it again.",
                          turbo_confirm_title: "Confirm apply",
                          turbo_confirm_button: "Apply",
                          turbo_confirm_variant: "primary" }
